# Romania (additions to data/extracted/ro/).

lg:RO-LCE
    lgo:shortName "L. 365/2002" ;
    eli:id_local "M.Of. nr. 483 din 5 iulie 2002" ;
    eli:transposes lg:EU-2000-31 ;
    rdfs:comment "Articolul 5 transposes Article 5 of the e-Commerce Directive, wider than the Directive's catalogue: phone and fax numbers, the fiscal registration code and price items are mandatory for every provider. In the consolidated text, alin. (1) lit. g) covers any regulated professional activity and alin. (3) — added by Legea nr. 50/2024 — requires the information to be kept up to date and usable by public authorities."@en .

# Round 6 additions: company-law information duty and the ADR trader-information
# duty, both rendered from legislatie.just.ro. Art. 74(5) is an express website
# clause; alin. (1)–(4) are the underlying document-information rules.

lg:RO-LEGA-31-1990 a lgo:LegalAct ;
    eli:title "Legea nr. 31 din 16 noiembrie 1990 privind societăţile"@ro , "Law No. 31 of 16 November 1990 on companies"@en ;
    lgo:shortName "Legea 31/1990" ;
    eli:transposes lg:EU-2017-1132 ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:SourceChecked ;
    rdfs:comment "Articolul 74(1) requires a company to state its name, legal form, seat, trade-register number and unique registration code on invoices, offers, orders, price lists, prospectuses and other documents used in commerce, and 74(5) extends the 74(1) and (3) information to the company's own website."@en .

lg:RO-OG-38-2015 a lgo:LegalAct ;
    eli:title "Ordonanța Guvernului nr. 38 din 26 august 2015 privind soluţionarea alternativă a litigiilor dintre consumatori şi comercianţi"@ro , "Government Ordinance No. 38 of 26 August 2015 on alternative dispute resolution for consumer disputes"@en ;
    lgo:shortName "O.G. 38/2015" ;
    eli:transposes lg:EU-2013-11 ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:SourceChecked .

# Legea 506/2004: the ePrivacy-sector act. Art. 4(5), (5¹)–(6) is the
# storage-and-access rule — ePrivacy Directive Art. 5(3) transposition as
# amended by OUG 13/2012: consent (acordul), GDPR-style information, consent
# via browser settings, plus the transmission/strictly-necessary exceptions.

lg:RO-LEGA-506 a lgo:LegalAct ;
    eli:title "Legea nr. 506 din 17 noiembrie 2004 privind prelucrarea datelor cu caracter personal şi protecţia vieţii private în sectorul comunicaţiilor electronice"@ro , "Law No. 506 of 17 November 2004 on the processing of personal data and the protection of privacy in the electronic communications sector"@en ;
    lgo:shortName "Legea 506/2004" ;
    lgo:actType lgv:Statute ;
    lgo:jurisdiction lg:RO ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://legislatie.just.ro/Public/DetaliiDocument/56973"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    eli:id_local "M.Of. nr. 237 din 18 noiembrie 2004" ;
    eli:transposes lg:EU-2002-58 ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:SourceChecked ;
    rdfs:comment "Articolul 4 alin. (5), (5¹)–(6), as amended by OUG nr. 13/2012 (in force 26-04-2012), permits storing information on, or accessing information stored on, a subscriber's or user's terminal equipment only with the cumulative satisfaction of: the subscriber's or user's consent (acordul), which may also be given through browser settings, and prior clear and complete information under art. 12 of Legea 677/2001 including the purpose of the processing (with a specific rule for third-party storage/access); alin. (6) excepts transmission-only storage/access and access strictly necessary for an expressly requested information-society service. Consent model."@en .
